    "content": "Eligible Trader Joe's shoppers who used a credit/debit card between March 5 and July 19, 2019, and received a receipt showing the first six and last four digits can claim a share of a $7.4 million settlement. Estimated payouts are ~$102.45. File a claim by June 9, 2026, via the official settlement website.Key Details on the Trader Joe's Class Action Settlement:Eligibility: You must have made a purchase at a Trader Joe's store between March 5, 2019, and July 19, 2019, using a credit or debit card and received a receipt displaying the first six and last four digits of the card number.Settlement Amount: The $7.4 million settlement aims to compensate shoppers for potential violations of the Fair and Accurate Credit Transactions Act (FACTA), which restricts printing excessive card information.Payout: The estimated payout is approximately $102.45 per claimant, depending on the final number of valid claims submitted.Deadline: Claims must be submitted by June 9, 2026.How to File:Online: Visit www.TJ-FACTASettlement.com.Phone: Call 1-888-444-7415.Class ID: A Class ID number, usually found on mailed or emailed notices, is required.A final approval hearing for the settlement is scheduled for August 10, 2026. If approved, checks are expected to be sent within 10 business days following the approval date.",
